  "findings": [
    "Both Visit constructors use the actual newborn Crossing and its two member edges, incoming old(j\u22121) and return new(j). Distinctness follows from old/new label disjointness. Finset membership proves these exhaust all visits of that crossing.",
    "The canonical visit parameters are identified with the frozen incoming and return Cramer parameters via actual crossing uniqueness under the explicit nonzero determinant. Strict interiority follows from enlarged G1; it is not an assumed bound.",
    "The incoming edge successor is old(j), the soft-edge successor is the return label, and those endpoints evaluate exactly to Pj and Pj+epsilon q. These statements include residue-zero insertion and expose the source path through both vertices.",
    "Each inherited visit is represented by its actual support partner. Frozen parameter windows and the canonical transported parameter formula give strict incoming-before-newborn and newborn-before-return inequalities. No new free parameter or visit map is introduced.",
    "An arbitrary child visit is either newborn or inherited by the exact support/visit range theorem. The two newborn visits are the arc endpoints, so neither is strictly between. Each inherited visit is excluded by ParentArc, using the proved parameter inequalities on either endpoint edge. This is an oriented traversalBetween assertion, including the numerical wrap.",
    "The common-radius result takes the minimum of transport/Generic, both finite windows and transversality radii. Every auxiliary premise is derived from parent Generic and SoftAdmissible. The loop proof remains inside the positive-epsilon quantifier; no enlarged Generic statement at epsilon zero is used.",
    "Root first40868 exited0, with all13 standard axiom traces and20 complete dependency body embeddings. First drafts equal the passing files. No proof repair or statement change was made."
  ],
